l look  the phone calls may be friendly and  congratulatory but the foreign policy is  anything but and that recent ICBM test  that you were just showing pictures of  emphasizes where we are in the  relationship the US has been accusing  Russia going back to the Obama  of cheating on nuclear arms-control  agreements specifically this treaty  called the INF treaty basically  developing these kind of missiles that  they had promised not to do and in in  response the Trump administration says  they're gonna start researching these  kind of missile development as well  breaking out of that sort of cap we had  on the nuclear arms race but when you  look at the national security team of  the trump administration they constantly  signal to our allies around the world  don't listen so much to what the  president saying look at what we're  doing and that's pretty significant to  have national security officials say  something like that look at what we're  doing in Ukraine look at what we're  doing with these expulsion don't worry  about the friendly phone calls all right  Margaret thank you so much and Sunday on  Face the Nation Margaret will talk with  Republican senator Tim Scott Republican  congressman trey Gowdy former Democratic  presidential candidate Bernie Sanders  and the UN High Commissioner for  Refugees all of that on Face the Nation  Sunday here on CBS
 

